// Runner self-test: packets keep the kernel's receive time. After the handshake (the
// shim warmed Zhida's ARP cache before the script), Zhida echoes 10 bytes about 2 ms
// after they arrive, while packetdrill sleeps until 0.05 s to send a duplicate ACK. The
// script expects the echo at 0.05 s, so packetdrill
// must report a timing error (run.c verify_time, 4 ms tolerance). A shim stamping packets
// when packetdrill reads them would stamp the echo at about 0.05 s and the script would
// pass. The duplicate ACK acknowledges nothing new and only makes packetdrill sleep.
// The peer omits timestamps, as in handshake-linux-options.pkt.
// expect-error: timing error: expected outbound packet at

0      < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0     > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0     < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0     < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 502
+0.05  < . 11:11(0) ack 1 win 502
+0     > P. 1:11(10) ack 11 win 32768
